/**
 * @defgroup MIDILAR_Midi Native MIDI 1.0 messages
 * @ingroup MIDILAR_Protocol
 * @brief Byte-oriented builders, adapted from the historical Message API.
 *
 * @section MIDILARMidiConcept Complete messages
 *
 * Message holds one complete short message in three inline bytes. Note On,
 * Note Off, AfterTouch, CC and Pitch Bend use three MIDI bytes. Program Change
 * and Channel Pressure use two. Real-time messages use one. The status byte
 * determines size(), so there is no allocation or separate size field.
 * SetRawData accepts one complete validated message, not a stream fragment.
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <MIDILAR_Protocol.h>
 * using MIDILAR::Protocol::Midi::Message;
 * Message msg;
 * msg.NoteOn(60, 100, 0); // wire channel 0 = human channel 1
 * // Send msg.Buffer(), msg.size() using the application's MIDI transport.
 * auto packet = MIDILAR::Protocol::Ump::Encode(MIDILAR::Protocol::Ump::Group::FromNumber(1), msg);
 * auto bytesAgain = MIDILAR::Protocol::Ump::DecodeMidi1(packet);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section MIDILARMidiStorage Storage and validity
 *
 * Builders mutate the object and return Message&. Invalid input clears it:
 * IsValid() is false, Buffer() is null and size() is zero. Data(index) returns
 * zero outside size(). A copy owns its three independent bytes.
 *
 * SysExMessage is different: it is a non-owning view of a caller buffer.
 * Copies alias the buffer. Keep it alive and unchanged for the entire view's
 * use. Build takes payload without F0/F7, validates all bytes and capacity,
 * and writes nothing on failure. There is no hidden allocation or truncation.
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * uint8_t storage[16];
 * const uint8_t payload[] = {0x7D, 1, 2, 3};
 * auto sysex = MIDILAR::Protocol::Midi::SysExMessage::Build(
 *     storage, sizeof(storage), payload, sizeof(payload));
 * // sysex.Buffer(): F0 7D 01 02 03 F7, size(): 6.
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section MIDILARMidiMigration Migration from MidiCore::Message
 *
 * - Include MIDILAR_Protocol.h and use MIDILAR::Protocol::Midi::Message.
 * - NoteOn, NoteOff, AfterTouch, ControlChange, ProgramChange, ChannelPressure,
 *   common CC helpers, transport and system-common builders retain their
 *   useful names and argument order. Channels remain wire indices 0-15.
 * - Invalid arguments are rejected instead of silently clamped. The current
 *   Channel wrapper still uses FromWire/FromNumber for explicit conversion.
 * - PitchBend always takes 0-16383. Use PitchBendSigned for -8192..8191 and
 *   PitchBend7 for 0-127. Overload resolution no longer changes the meaning.
 * - Replace dynamic SystemExclusive and MTC_FullFrame methods with
 *   SysExMessage::Build and SysExMessage::MTC_FullFrame using caller storage.
 * - Vector constructors, iterators and implicit ownership are not retained.
 * - The old NRPN helpers were empty. Compose CC 99/98 and Data Entry 6/38
 *   explicitly; see @ref MIDI_NRPN_MESSAGES. One Message holds one CC.
 * - Ump::Midi1Parser and the existing devices continue to use Ump::Packet. Construction
 *   and raw-byte access need no UMP conversion. Ump::Encode requires an explicit
 *   group and normalizes velocity-zero Note On; Ump::DecodeMidi1 accepts short MIDI
 *   1.0 UMP only, discards its group and never downconverts MIDI 2.0.
 * - This is an adapted API, not binary or source compatibility with the
 *   removed implementation. See SPEC-M1-1..4 in @ref MIDILAR_Specification.
 *
 * @see MIDI_Protocol
 */
